        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7d5d4648-c6f4-5af3-9cff-30528d467dae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Into the Homeland\n- People: Lesli Linka Glatter, Powers Boothe, C. Thomas Howell, Paul LeMat, Cindy Pickett, Jim Jones, Philip Marlowe, Cy Tolliver, Curly Bill Brocious, Noah Daniels, Lamar Wyatt\n- Organizations: HBO\n- Topics: television crime drama roles\n\nFacts:\n- Into the Homeland is a 1987 made-for-TV crime drama.\n- Into the Homeland aired on HBO on December 26, 1987.\n- Lesli Linka Glatter directed Into the Homeland.\n- Powers Boothe, C. Thomas Howell, Paul LeMat, and Cindy Pickett starred in Into the Homeland.\n- Powers Boothe had an Emmy-winning portrayal of Jim Jones.\n- Powers Boothe played TV detective Philip Marlowe in the 1980s.\n- Powers Boothe played Cy Tolliver on Deadwood.\n- Powers Boothe played Curly Bill Brocious in Tombstone.\n- Powers Boothe played Vice-President and later President Noah Daniels on 24.\n- Powers Boothe played Lamar Wyatt in Nashville.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
